# =============================================================================
# RC Knowledge Platform — environment variables
# =============================================================================

# --- Local development (default) ---
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=file:./data/local.db
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN is not needed for local SQLite

# --- Vercel production (required) ---
# Create a database at https://turso.tech (free tier works for demos).
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-database-name-your-org.turso.io
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-turso-auth-token

# Tip: install the Turso integration in the Vercel dashboard — it sets both vars automatically.

# --- Deployment ---
# Vercel runs `npm run vercel-build`, which pushes schema then builds the app.
# GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/db-schema.yml`) also pushes schema when
# `lib/db/schema.ts` changes on `main` (requires repo secrets below).
#
# GitHub repository secrets (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions):
#   TURSO_DATABASE_URL
#   TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN
#
# Seed is NOT run automatically — run `npm run db:seed` once manually for a new DB.

# --- Static demo content in pages ---
# UI demo/seeded catalog displays are disabled via `config/demo-display.ts`
# (`RENDER_STATIC_DEMO_DATA = false`). Set to `true` to restore fixture-backed
# page content. Fixture files under `data/fixtures/` are unchanged and used by seed scripts.
